  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Extended stretch of dry weather with minor wind \nimpacts from Nor'easter this weekend\n\nAnother chilly late September night particularly across the\nnorthern and western Alleghenies where patchy frost is likely in\nthe usual cold spots. Coordinated with PBZ and LWX on a frost \nadvisory for Somerset County. Added McKean and Potter Counties\nto the frost advisory this evening with temps already falling \ninto the upper 30s to mid 40s at 8 PM, increasing the \nlikelihood of frost later tonight.\n\nA much needed break from the rain (following one of the wettest\nmid to late summer patterns on record) is expected over the \nnext 7 days across the majority of central PA. \n\nA Nor'easter developing offshore NJ/Long Island/southern New \nEngland could bring some light rain to the eastern third of the \nCWA (mainly east of US-15) later this weekend (20-40 PoPs Sat,\n40-60 PoPs Sun). Breezy conditions are expected Saturday and \nSunday with max gusts 30-35 mph over the higher terrain in the \nnortheast portion of the forecast area. \n\nAs the Nor'Easter moves toward the Canadian Maritimes, \ntemperatures are projected to rebound and climb several degrees \nabove the historical average by the middle and latter part of\nthe week.",
